cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Scheduler Is an Interaction Designer: a benchmark for serving-layer effects on turn-taking in mixed-initiative human-AI teams"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Syeda Shafia
    family-names: Rubbani
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2535-7463"
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/mias-bench"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark and reference implementation for studying how LLM
  serving mechanics - KV-cache residency, continuous batching and preemption -
  shape the realised turn order of multi-agent mixed-initiative systems, and
  whether an interaction-aware scheduler can restore the designed order at
  bounded throughput cost.
keywords:
  - human-AI collaboration
  - mixed-initiative systems
  - LLM serving
  - vLLM
  - scheduling
  - agency
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
